# Frontend Patterns

`@furystack/eslint-plugin` enforces most Shade render-time conventions — generate compliant code from the start.

## Lint enforces

| Topic | Rule |
|---|---|
| No module-level JSX | `no-module-level-jsx` |
| No manual `.subscribe()` in render | `no-manual-subscribe-in-render` |
| No `.getValue()` without `useObservable` | `no-direct-get-value-in-render` |
| Prefer `useState` over manual `ObservableValue` | `prefer-use-state` |
| No `useState` for CSS states | `no-css-state-hooks` |
| Valid `customElementName` | `valid-custom-element-name` |
| `LocationService` + `NestedRouteLink` for navigation | `prefer-location-service`, `prefer-nested-route-link` |
| `tabindex` with spatial nav targets | `require-tabindex-with-spatial-nav-target` |

## Service-based data access (NEVER fetch from components)

Always go through a service that wraps `Cache`. Components subscribe to the cache observable.

```typescript
// ✅ service token wrapping an Impl class (see CODE_STYLE.mdc for the pattern)
import { Cache } from '@furystack/cache'
import { defineService, type Token } from '@furystack/inject'
import { IdentityApiClient } from './api-clients/identity-api-client.js'

class UsersServiceImpl implements Disposable {
  public userCache = new Cache({
    capacity: 100,
    load: async (username: string) => {
      const { result } = await this.identityApiClient.call({
        method: 'GET',
        action: '/users/:id',
        url: { id: username },
        query: {},
      })
      return result
    },
  })

  public userQueryCache = new Cache({
    capacity: 10,
    load: async (findOptions: FindOptions<User, Array<keyof User>>) => {
      const { result } = await this.identityApiClient.call({ method: 'GET', action: '/users', query: { findOptions } })
      // populate individual cache from list results
      result.entries.forEach((entry) => {
        this.userCache.setExplicitValue({
          loadArgs: [entry.username],
          value: { status: 'loaded', value: entry, updatedAt: new Date() },
        })
      })
      return result
    },
  })

  constructor(private readonly identityApiClient: IdentityApiClient) {}

  public getUser = this.userCache.get.bind(this.userCache)
  public getUserAsObservable = this.userCache.getObservable.bind(this.userCache)
  public findUsers = this.userQueryCache.get.bind(this.userQueryCache)

  public updateUser = async (username: string, body: UserUpdate) => {
    const { result } = await this.identityApiClient.call({ method: 'PATCH', action: '/users/:id', url: { id: username }, body })
    await this.userCache.reload(username)   // see TESTING_GUIDELINES.mdc — await the reload
    this.userQueryCache.flushAll()
    return result
  }

  public [Symbol.dispose](): void {
    this.userCache[Symbol.dispose]()
    this.userQueryCache[Symbol.dispose]()
  }
}

export type UsersService = UsersServiceImpl

export const UsersService: Token<UsersService, 'singleton'> = defineService({
  name: 'pi-rat/UsersService',
  lifetime: 'singleton',
  factory: ({ inject, onDispose }) => {
    const impl = new UsersServiceImpl(inject(IdentityApiClient))
    // eslint-disable-next-line furystack/prefer-using-wrapper -- Disposal deferred to injector tear-down
    onDispose(() => impl[Symbol.dispose]())
    return impl
  },
})
```

```typescript
// ✅ component subscribes via getObservable
const UserDisplay = Shade<{ username: string }>({
  customElementName: 'user-display',
  render: ({ props, injector, useObservable }) => {
    const usersService = injector.get(UsersService)
    const [state] = useObservable('user', usersService.getUserAsObservable(props.username))

    if (state.status === 'loading') return <div>Loading...</div>
    if (state.status === 'failed') return <div>Error: {String(state.error)}</div>
    if (state.status === 'loaded') return <div>{state.value.username}</div>
    return null
  },
})

// ❌ never fetch directly in a component
render: ({ injector }) => {
  const apiClient = injector.get(IdentityApiClient)
  void apiClient.call({ /* ... */ })   // no caching, duplicate requests, leaks
}
```

For detailed `Cache` patterns (capacity, query caches, `setExplicitValue`, error handling) see `CACHE_HANDLING.mdc`.

## Cross-component state — shared services, not prop drilling

If state is shared across 3+ component levels or sibling components, lift it into a `defineService` token exposing observables. Keep props for simple display data and parent callbacks.

```typescript
// ✅ shared state behind a service token
class RoleEditorStateImpl implements Disposable {
  public originalRoles = new ObservableValue<Roles>([])
  public currentRoles = new ObservableValue<Roles>([])
  public isModified = new ObservableValue(false)

  public addRole = (role: Roles[number]) => {
    const current = this.currentRoles.getValue()
    if (!current.includes(role)) {
      this.currentRoles.setValue([...current, role])
      this.updateModifiedState()
    }
  }

  public [Symbol.dispose](): void {
    this.originalRoles[Symbol.dispose]()
    this.currentRoles[Symbol.dispose]()
    this.isModified[Symbol.dispose]()
  }
  // ...
}

export type RoleEditorState = RoleEditorStateImpl

export const RoleEditorState: Token<RoleEditorState, 'singleton'> = defineService({
  name: 'pi-rat/RoleEditorState',
  lifetime: 'singleton',
  factory: ({ onDispose }) => {
    const impl = new RoleEditorStateImpl()
    // eslint-disable-next-line furystack/prefer-using-wrapper -- Disposal deferred to injector tear-down
    onDispose(() => impl[Symbol.dispose]())
    return impl
  },
})
```

| Scenario | Approach |
|---|---|
| Simple display data | props are fine |
| Callback for parent | props are fine |
| Data needed 3+ levels deep | shared service token |
| Complex interdependent state | shared service token |
| Shared across siblings | shared service token |

## Routing — `navigateToRoute()` only

```typescript
import type { Route } from '@furystack/shades'
import { PiRatLazyLoad } from '../pirat-lazy-load.js'

export const userDetailsRoute = {
  url: '/users/:username',
  onVisit, onLeave,
  component: ({ match }) => (
    <PiRatLazyLoad
      component={async () => {
        const { UserDetails } = await import('../../pages/admin/user-details.js')
        return <UserDetails username={match.params.username} />
      }}
    />
  ),
} satisfies Route<{ username: string }>

// In a handler:
import { navigateToRoute } from '../navigate-to-route.js'

navigateToRoute(injector, userDetailsRoute, { username: 'alice' })
```

Never manipulate `window.history` or call `injector.get(LocationService)` directly in a component for navigation — bypasses route system, no type safety.

## Component pattern

```typescript
const MyComponent = Shade<{ id: string }>({
  customElementName: 'my-component',
  render: ({ props, injector, useObservable, useDisposable }) => {
    // services
    const session = injector.get(SessionService)

    // global state
    const [user] = useObservable('user', session.currentUser)

    // local reactive state — pair with useObservable to trigger re-renders
    const isLoadingObs = useDisposable('isLoading', () => new ObservableValue(false))
    const [isLoading] = useObservable('isLoadingValue', isLoadingObs)

    return <div>{/* ... */}</div>
  },
})
```

Reading observables with `.getValue()` directly in render does **not** subscribe — UI won't react. Always pair `useDisposable` with `useObservable` for reactive reads.

## DOM access — `element` from render context

Pi-rat's Shades version exposes `element` in render args. Use `element.querySelector(...)` for shadow-DOM-aware queries. Never use global `document.querySelector` — bypasses shadow DOM boundaries.

```typescript
render: ({ element }) => {
  const handleSubmit = () => {
    const form = element.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('form[data-my-form]')
    form?.reset()
  }
  return <form data-my-form>{/* ... */}</form>
}
```

Prefer state-driven re-renders (`key` increment to remount, ObservableValue toggles) over imperative DOM mutations when possible.

## Forms

```typescript
const MyForm = Shade({
  customElementName: 'my-form',
  render: ({ injector, useDisposable, useObservable }) => {
    const service = injector.get(MyService)
    const isLoadingObs = useDisposable('loading', () => new ObservableValue(false))
    const errorObs = useDisposable('error', () => new ObservableValue(''))
    const [isLoading] = useObservable('loadingValue', isLoadingObs)
    const [error] = useObservable('errorValue', errorObs)

    const handleSubmit = async (data: FormPayload) => {
      // client-side validation only
      if (data.field1 !== data.field2) {
        errorObs.setValue('Fields must match')
        return
      }
      isLoadingObs.setValue(true)
      errorObs.setValue('')
      try {
        await service.performAction(data)
      } catch (err) {
        errorObs.setValue(err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Operation failed')
      } finally {
        isLoadingObs.setValue(false)
      }
    }

    return (
      <Form<FormPayload>
        validate={(d): d is FormPayload => !!(d?.field1?.length && d?.field2?.length)}
        onSubmit={(d) => void handleSubmit(d)}
      >
        <Input name="field1" required />
        {error && <ErrorDisplay message={error} />}
        <Button type="submit" disabled={isLoading}>
          {isLoading ? 'Processing...' : 'Submit'}
        </Button>
      </Form>
    )
  },
})
```

## Styling — CSS variables for theme

```typescript
style={{
  backgroundColor: 'var(--theme-background-default)',
  color: 'var(--theme-text-primary)',
  border: '1px solid var(--theme-border-default)',
  borderRadius: '8px',
}}
```

Layout patterns: settings pages centered max-width 800px, forms max-width 400px, dropdowns absolute-positioned with click-outside overlay, 44px minimum touch targets.

## UI feature entry points

When adding a new feature page, **ask the user** which entry points to add. Don't add them all by default.

| Entry Point | File | Access | Use case |
|---|---|---|---|
| Avatar Menu | `user-avatar-menu.tsx` | role-based | user/admin actions, settings, logout |
| Command Palette | `command-palette/command-providers/<x>.tsx` | role-based in provider | quick navigation, search, actions |
| App Shortcut Widget | `dashboard/app-shortcut-widget.tsx` | dashboard owner/admin | dashboard shortcut to app pages |
| Entity Shortcut Widget | `dashboard/entity-shortcut-widget.tsx` | dashboard owner/admin | dashboard shortcut to entity pages |
| App Bar | `layout.tsx` | visibility-based | global navigation (rarely needed) |
| Default Dashboard Patch | DB seed / migration | all users | pre-configured widgets |

### Avatar menu

```typescript
{isAdmin && (
  <Button onclick={() => { navigateToRoute(injector, myFeatureRoute, {}); setIsMenuOpen(false) }}>
    🔧 My Feature
  </Button>
)}
```

### Command palette provider

Author a `CommandProvider` in `command-palette/command-providers/<feature>.tsx`. Score full hits 1, prefix 2, contains 3. Apply role check inside the provider when needed. Register in `command-palette/index.tsx`.

### App shortcut widget

1. Add the new app name to `common/src/models/dashboard/app-shortcut-widget.ts` union
2. Add a case to `frontend/src/components/dashboard/app-shortcut-widget.tsx` returning an `IconUrlWidget` with the route URL and icon

## Access control

| Pattern | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Admin-only | `isAdmin && <Button>` or `roles?.includes('admin')` |
| Authenticated | `currentUser && <Button>` |
| Public | always render |
| Role-based | `roles?.includes('role')` |
